# AD-22 reconcile/liveness sweep — the chosen mechanism: system cron hitting the authenticated
# localhost admin endpoint. No always-on Python scheduler process competing for RAM (AD-21).
#
# Install with:  crontab -l 2>/dev/null | cat - deploy/reconcile.cron | crontab -
#
# Every 15 minutes: alert on stale parked/error runs (once per threshold) and reconcile-poll the two
# gate tickets, recovering any gate-Done a dropped webhook missed. This adds recoverability, NOT a
# timeout — parked runs still park indefinitely (AD-22).
#
# The token is read out of /opt/agent/.env at run time rather than written here, for two reasons:
# cron runs with a near-empty environment (a bare `${ADMIN_API_TOKEN}` would expand to nothing and
# every sweep would 401 silently), and a crontab is world-readable — the secret stays in the .env,
# which is not. `grep|cut` rather than sourcing the file, so a value containing spaces or shell
# metacharacters cannot be executed.
#
# `tr -d '\042\047\r'` strips surrounding quotes and a CRLF line ending. Octal (\042 = ", \047 = ')
# rather than the literal characters: nesting quotes inside a single-quoted crontab command is what
# turns a small edit into `tr -d` silently eating every letter of the token.
*/15 * * * * T=$(grep -m1 '^ADMIN_API_TOKEN=' /opt/agent/.env | cut -d= -f2- | tr -d '\042\047\r') && curl -fsS -m 60 -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/admin/reconcile -H "X-Admin-Token: $T" >> /var/log/agent-reconcile.log 2>&1
